@template steady
// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: crew comment when you wear dirty clothes. clothes.remark: yesterday's clothes
// (flag:clothes.stale); clothes.grubby: a grubby uniform (flag:clothes.grubby, AC3). Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
// Kind, never mean: the joke is on the clothes, not on you.
== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- That's yesterday's shirt. Change when you get a minute.
- Same clothes as yesterday? Easy fix. Wardrobe.
? flag:clothes.stale tier>=friend
- Everyone runs out once. The laundry sorts it.   #warm
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- You've worked hard. Your uniform says so.
- Grime on you. Change before you sit down to eat.
? flag:clothes.grubby tier>=friend
- Good shift? Change, wash, then eat. In that order.   #warm

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more lines for the chat card's opener (greet, near), so a tap doesn't repeat.
// Heard after a person's own lines are used up (FX13's no-repeat). {hi}, {nick} and {me} are the speaker's own words.
== greet
- {hi}. Nice to run into you.
- {hi}. How's the day treating you?
- {hi}, {nick}. All going well?
- Hello. Got a minute? I've got a few.
- {hi}. You look like you've been busy.
- {hi}. Things ticking along your end?
- {hi}. Glad you stopped by.
- {hi}. Take a seat if you like.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. You've a knack for good timing.
- {hi}. You've settled in well. People say so.
? time:morning
- Morning. Steady start. That's the best kind.
? time:evening
- Evening. Nice to stop for a bit, isn't it?
== near
- Just finishing this. Won't be long.
- {room}. I like it when it's tidy.
- Slow and steady. That's the way.
- Every job's easy once you've done it a few times.
- Pass me that, would you? Thanks.
- No rush. It'll get done.
- Doing it properly. Takes a little longer.
- Nearly there. Then I'm all ears.
